# This directory is a **bench**, not an application: only the overlay is in the repository.
#
# An installed Magento distribution weighs 769 MB, 626 of them for `vendor/`. Once
# `vendor/` is excluded by the root `.gitignore`, there are still **10,178 files**
# that composer wrote — `dev/` alone brings 7,256. None of that is code of this
# repository, and tracking it would amount to versioning Mage-OS.
#
# So the rule is inverted: everything is ignored, and the overlay re-allows itself
# by name. A file composer adds tomorrow stays out without anyone having to think
# about it — which is what an exclusion list cannot do.
#
# What the overlay contains, and why it is in the repository:
#   composer.json / composer.lock  the path repositories towards src/, and the
#                                  Mage-OS pin that makes the install reproducible
#   compose.yaml                   MySQL, OpenSearch, Redis, Temporal, its UI
#   check-php-extensions.sh        what the host must have before trying
#   auth.json.sample               Mage-OS does not ask for one; the sample says
#                                  what to put for a distribution that does
#   .env.example                   the variables compose.yaml expects
#   README.md                      how to bootstrap, and what it is pinned on
#   probe-lock.php                 the §1.4 probe: is the lock shared between
#                                  processes? It replays on another host, whose
#                                  `lock.provider` may differ
#   probe-queue.php                the §1.3 probe: what does a consumer that dies
#                                  in the middle of a message leave behind?
#   probe-resume.php               the §5.3 probe: does a command killed midway
#                                  resume without charging the card again?
#   probe-order.php                the §5.2 probe: does a placed order start an
#                                  execution on the cluster?
#   probe-cases.php                the observation screen probe: an execution that
#                                  holds every case the page must know how to
#                                  show — failure, timer, child, resume
#   app/code/Gplanchat/DurableProbe the bench module. It carries the
#                                  **demonstration** — `PlaceOrderWorkflow`,
#                                  `durable:demo` — and the queue topics of the
#                                  probes. None of that belongs in the published
#                                  package: an integration module must not make a
#                                  project carry workflows that are not its own.
#
# `sylius/` does the opposite — an exclusion list — because over there the
# application skeleton **is** project code: 220 files written here. Here there are
# six, and ten thousand that are not.
*
!.gitignore
!composer.json
!composer.lock
!compose.yaml
!check-php-extensions.sh
!auth.json.sample
!.env.example
!README.md
!probe-lock.php
!probe-queue.php
!probe-resume.php
!probe-order.php
!probe-cases.php

# The probe module, and it alone: `app/etc/env.php` and the rest of `app/`
# stay out. Every level re-allows itself, because `*` excludes at all of them.
!app/
!app/code/
!app/code/Gplanchat/
!app/code/Gplanchat/DurableProbe/
!app/code/Gplanchat/DurableProbe/**

# The conformance harness (#747): PHPUnit runs from the repository's own vendor/, so the bench
# adds no dependency.
!phpunit.xml.dist
!tests/
!tests/**
